{"id": 1013139, "slug": "evil-egg-2", "name": "Evil Egg", "name_original": "Evil Egg", "description": "<h3>I NEVER WANTED TO BE BORN A MONSTER</h3><p><strong>Evil Egg</strong> was an ecstatic twin-stick nightmare known for its <strong>brutal shooting action </strong>and <strong>intense audiovisual effects.</strong> Infinite horrors tear apart a world of little green men, the only hope an errant hatchling.</p><p>The last known <strong>Evil Egg </strong>arcade<strong> </strong>cabinet to remain was recovered in Eugene, Oregon, found in a state of extreme disrepair. This digital release is a faithful emulation of the original hardware, made possible by a restoration effort led by a small team of dedicated preservationists. The private collector responsible for the machine's donation has asked to remain anonymous.</p><h3>FEATURES</h3><ul><li><p><strong>CLASSIC, FULLY ANALOG TWIN-STICK BLASTING</strong></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>UNIQUE ASSORTMENT OF ENEMIES, HAZARDS, POWERUPS AND ARTEFACTS</strong></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>INFINITE LEVELS IF YOU CAN REACH THEM</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>SCORE SYSTEM REWARDING SKILL AND FUN</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>ONLINE LEADERBOARDS</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>LOOKS LIKE CANDY</strong></p></li></ul><p><strong>PHOTOSENSITIVITY WARNING: This game contains flashing lights and intense strobe effects.</strong> </p>", "metacritic": null, "metacritic_platforms": [], "released": "2025-10-30", "tba": false, "updated": "2025-10-31T07:21:26", "background_image": "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/91b/91bd676922a7f8027380eb88a9b557fe.jpg", "background_image_additional": "https://media.rawg.io/media/screenshots/87a/87af3bfba1cc919501d74d26a4c6db06.jpg", "website": "https://ivysly.com/games/evil-egg.html", "rating": 0.0, "rating_top": 0, "ratings": [], "reactions": null, "added": 3, "added_by_status": {"yet": 2, "toplay": 1}, "playtime": 0, "screenshots_count": 11, "movies_count": 0, "creators_count": 0, "achievemen